
## Environment Variables

All configuration is done via environment variables. See `.env.example` for a complete list. Key variables:

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `POSTGRES_DB`, `POSTGRES_USER`, `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` | Database credentials |
| `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` | Django secret key |
| `DEBUG` | Set to `1` for development |
| `ADMIN_USERNAME`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `ADMIN_EMAIL` | Default admin account |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | Google OAuth2 credentials |
| `FACEBOOK_APP_ID`, `FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET` | Facebook app credentials |
| `INSTAGRAM_APP_ID`, `INSTAGRAM_APP_SECRET` | Instagram app credentials |
| `NEXTCLOUD_URL`, `NEXTCLOUD_USERNAME`, `NEXTCLOUD_PASSWORD`, `NEXTCLOUD_FOLDER` | Nextcloud WebDAV settings |
| `GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_DRIVE_TOKEN`, `GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID` | Google Drive API settings |
| `REDIS_HOST`, `REDIS_PORT` | Redis connection (default: `redis`, `6379`) |
| `EMAIL_BACKEND`, `EMAIL_HOST`, ... | Email configuration (console backend for dev) |
| `FRONTEND_URL` | Public URL of the frontend (for email links) |
| `VITE_API_URL` | API base URL for frontend (empty in Docker) |
| `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | Google client ID for frontend |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Backend log level (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR) |
| `VITE_LOG_LEVEL` | Frontend log level (debug, info, warn, error) |

